<title>NETHERLANDS: Vredestein buys Dunlop boots unit.</title>
<headline>Vredestein buys Dunlop boots unit.</headline>
<dateline>VELP, Netherlands 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tyre and rubber products maker Vredestein NV said on Monday it had successfully concluded the previously announced takeover of the rubber boots business of British firm Dunlop Footwear.</p>
<p>Dunlop's rubber boots unit is based near Liverpool, England, and employs 90 people. It will be bought by the end of this year by Vredestein's rubber boots subsidiary Hevea, which has 250 employees in the Netherlands and Portugal.</p>
<p>Vredestein said the takeover, of which no financial details were disclosed, would considerably strengthen its market position in Europe and in Britain in particular.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
